      "index": "b0H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1561602059,
      "version": 172,
      "versionNonce": 1039319557,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793911530342,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Explanation of Commands\nCommand        Meaning\naddgroup        Creates a new group.\n--system        Creates a system group/user.\n--gid 1001        Assigns Group ID 1001.\nadduser        Creates a new user.\n--uid 1001        Assigns User ID 1001.\nUSER nodejs        Switches from root to the nodejs user.\nCMD        Executes the application startup command.\n\nImportant Concepts\n- UID (User ID): Unique numeric identifier assigned to a user.\n- GID (Group ID): Unique numeric identifier assigned to a group.\n- Non-root user: A user without root-level administrative privileges.\n- Least Privilege Principle: Give users only the permissions required to\nperform their tasks.",
      "rawText": "Explanation of Commands\nCommand        Meaning\naddgroup        Creates a new group.\n--system        Creates a system group/user.\n--gid 1001        Assigns Group ID 1001.\nadduser        Creates a new user.\n--uid 1001        Assigns User ID 1001.\nUSER nodejs        Switches from root to the nodejs user.\nCMD        Executes the application startup command.\n\nImportant Concepts\n- UID (User ID): Unique numeric identifier assigned to a user.\n- GID (Group ID): Unique numeric identifier assigned to a group.\n- Non-root user: A user without root-level administrative privileges.\n- Least Privilege Principle: Give users only the permissions required to perform their tasks.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Explanation of Commands\nCommand        Meaning\naddgroup        Creates a new group.\n--system        Creates a system group/user.\n--gid 1001        Assigns Group ID 1001.\nadduser        Creates a new user.\n--uid 1001        Assigns User ID 1001.\nUSER nodejs        Switches from root to the nodejs user.\nCMD        Executes the application startup command.\n\nImportant Concepts\n- UID (User ID): Unique numeric identifier assigned to a user.\n- GID (Group ID): Unique numeric identifier assigned to a group.\n- Non-root user: A user without root-level administrative privileges.\n- Least Privilege Principle: Give users only the permissions required to perform their tasks.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "link": null
    }
  ],
